Keeps a page's beforeunload answer awaited across a same-document commit (#3920). A step back or
forward to a same-document entry, as a page's own history router makes, commits in the current
frame host, and CommitNavigation reset its waiting state first, so a tab's close or the browser's
quit waiting on that page stopped its 500 ms timer and dropped the page's answer: the first Quit
or ⌘W did nothing. A same-document commit now leaves the wait, its timer and the round's dialog
state alone; a cross-document commit resets them as before. Chromium's main has the same reset
today.

--- a/content/browser/renderer_host/render_frame_host_impl.cc
+++ b/content/browser/renderer_host/render_frame_host_impl.cc
@@ -12850,7 +12850,13 @@
 
   // Get back to a clean state, in case we start a new navigation without
   // completing an unload handler.
-  ResetWaitingState();
+  // ilo: a same-document commit keeps its document, so a beforeunload it is
+  // still answering, for a tab's close or the browser's quit, stays awaited
+  // and timed. Resetting here dropped that answer, and the close never came
+  // (#3920).
+  if (!is_same_document) {
+    ResetWaitingState();
+  }
 
   // The renderer can exit view source mode when any error or cancellation
   // happen. When reusing the same renderer, overwrite to recover the mode.
